hadiths[14]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27766","Haddathana Yunus who said: Haddathana Layth from Abu Wahb al-Khawlani from a man he named from Abu Basra al-Ghifari, companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I asked my Lord, mighty and majestic, for four, and He gave me three and barred me one; I asked Allah, mighty and majestic, not to unite my umma upon misguidance, and He gave it to me; and I asked Allah, mighty and majestic, not to destroy them by years as He destroyed the nations before them, and He gave it to me; and I asked Allah, mighty and majestic, not to clothe them in sects and make some taste the violence of others, and He barred me it."
"27767","Haddathana Yaqub who said: Haddathana my father from Ibn Ishaq who said: Haddathani Yazid ibn Habib from Khayr ibn Nuaym al-Hadrami from Abd Allah ibn Hubayra al-Sabai, and he was trustworthy, from Abu Tamim from Abu Basra al-Ghifari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in Asr prayer, and when he left he said: Indeed this prayer was offered to those before you, and they were heedless in it and left it; so whoever of you prays it, his reward is doubled twofold; and there is no prayer after it until the witness is seen, and the witness is the star."
"27768","Haddathana Yahya ibn Ishaq who said: Akhbarana Ibn Lahia from Abd Allah ibn Hubayra from Abu Tamim al-Jayshani from Abu Basra al-Ghifari who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when I emigrated, and that was before I embraced Islam; so he milked for me a small ewe which he used to milk for his family, and I drank it; so when morning came I embraced Islam; and the family of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We spend the night tonight as we spent last night, hungry; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) milked for me a sheep and I drank it and was satisfied; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Are you satisfied; so I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am satisfied; I neither ate to satiety nor drank to satisfaction before today; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the disbeliever eats in seven intestines and the believer eats in one intestine."
"27769","Haddathana Yahya ibn Ishaq who said: Akhbarana Ibn Lahia from Abd Allah ibn Hubayra from Abu Tamim from Abu Basra al-Ghifari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in a valley of their valleys called al-Mukhammas in Asr prayer, so he said: Indeed this prayer, the Asr prayer, was offered to those before you and they wasted it; indeed whoever prays it, his reward is doubled twice; indeed there is no prayer after it until you see the witness; I said to Ibn Lahia: What is the witness; he said: The star; the Arabs call the star the witness of the night."
"27770","Haddathana Yahya ibn Ishaq: Akhbarani Layth ibn Sad from Khayr ibn Nuaym from Abd Allah from Abu Tamim al-Jayshani from Abu Basra al-Ghifari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer, and he mentioned it."
"27771","Haddathana Yahya ibn Ishaq: Akhbarana Ibn Lahia: Akhbarana Abd Allah ibn Hubayra who said: I heard Abu Tamim al-Jayshani say: I heard Amr ibn al-As say: A man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed me, saying: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, mighty and majestic, has added a prayer for you, so pray it between the Isha prayer and the Subh prayer, al-Witr, al-Witr; indeed he is Abu Basra al-Ghifari; Abu Tamim said: So I and Abu Dharr were sitting; he said: So Abu Dharr took my hand and we went to Abu Basra and found him at the door next to the house of Amr ibn al-As; so Abu Dharr said: O Abu Basra, did you hear the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed Allah, mighty and majestic, has added a prayer for you, pray it between the Isha prayer and the Subh prayer, al-Witr, al-Witr; he said: Yes; he said: Did you hear it; he said: Yes; he said: Did you hear it; he said: Yes."
"27772","Haddathana Yaqub who said: Haddathana my father from Ibn Ishaq who said: Haddathani Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Marthad ibn Abd Allah al-Yazani from Abu Basra al-Ghifari who said: I met Abu Hurayra while he was traveling to the mosque of al-Tur to pray in it; he said: So I said to him: If I had met you before you departed, you would not have departed; he said: So he said: And why; he said: He said: So I said: Indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Mounts are not saddled except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, the Farthest Mosque, and my mosque."
"27773","Haddathana Hajjaj and Yunus who said: Haddathana al-Layth who said: Haddathani Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Abu al-Khayr from Mansur al-Kalbi from Dihya ibn Khalifa that he went out from his village to near the village of Uqba in Ramadan, then he broke his fast and people with him broke their fast, and others disliked to break their fast; he said: So when he returned to his village he said: By Allah, I have seen today a matter I never thought I would see; indeed a people have turned away from the guidance of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions; he says that to those who fasted; then he said at that: O Allah, take me to You."
"27774","Haddathana Abu Abd al-Rahman who said: Haddathana Said ibn Abi Ayyub who said: Haddathani Yazid ibn Abi Habib that Kulayb ibn Dhuhl informed him from Ubayd, meaning Ibn Jabr, who said: I rode with Abu Basra al-Ghifari, companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in a ship from al-Fustat in Ramadan, and it pushed off, then he brought his lunch near, then said: Come near; so I said: Do we not see the houses; so Abu Basra said: Have you turned away from the sunna of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"27775","Haddathana Attab who said: Haddathana Abd Allah who said: Haddathana Said ibn Yazid from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Kulayb ibn Dhuhl from Ubayd ibn Jabr who said: I rode with Abu Basra from al-Fustat to Alexandria in a ship, and when we pushed off from our anchorage he ordered his food and it was brought near, then he called me to lunch, and that was in Ramadan; so I said: O Abu Basra, by Allah our dwellings have not yet disappeared from us; so he said: Do you turn away from the sunna of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I said: No; he said: Then eat; so we remained breaking our fast until we reached our destination."
"27776","Haddathana Yahya ibn Ghaylan who said: Haddathana al-Mufaddal who said: Haddathana Abd Allah ibn Ayyash from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Kulayb ibn Dhuhl al-Hadrami from Ubayd ibn Jabr who said: I rode with Abu Basra in the ship while he was heading to Alexandria, and he mentioned the hadith."
"27777","Haddathana Abu Asim from Abd al-Hamid, meaning Ibn Jafar, who said: Akhbarani Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Marthad ibn Abd Allah from Abu Basra al-Ghifari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them one day: Indeed I am riding to the Jews, so whoever goes with me, if they greet you then say: And upon you; so we went, and when we came to them and they greeted us, we said: And upon you."
"27778","Haddathana Hasan: Haddathana Ibn Lahia who said: Haddathana Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Abu al-Khayr who said: I heard Abu Basra say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed we are going to the Jews tomorrow, so do not initiate them with greeting; and when they greet you, say: And upon you."
"27779","Haddathana Waki who said: Haddathana Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Mirthad ibn Abd Allah from Abu Basra who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed we are going to the Jews tomorrow, so do not initiate them with greeting; and when they greet you, say: And upon you."
